{"availability":"available","full":"AI-SDC/ACRO","name":"ACRO","description":"Tools for the Semi-Automatic Checking of Research Outputs. These are tools for researchers to use as drop-in replacements for common analysis commands.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":27,"forks":12,"created":"2022-09-08T11:05:51Z","updated":"2026-10-05T17:48:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["data-privacy","data-protection","privacy","privacy-tools","statistical-disclosure-control","statistical-software"],"demo":"https://mybinder.org/v2/gh/AI-SDC/ACRO/main?urlpath=/lab/tree/notebooks/acro_demo_2026.ipynb","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:27.981Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:27.981Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:27.981Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T18:32:56.303Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:38.992Z","stars":27,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:48.466Z","stars":27,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-05T18:32:56.303Z","stars":27,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-07T18:42:36.142Z","stars":27,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-09T19:33:27.981Z","stars":27,"forks":12}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["ACRO is a free and open source tool that supports the semi-automated checking of research outputs (SACRO) for privacy disclosure within secure data environments. SACRO is a framework that applies best-practice principles-based statistical disclosure control (SDC) techniques on-the-fly as researchers conduct their analysis. SACRO is designed to assist human checkers rather than seeking to replace them as with current automated rules-based approaches.","The ACRO package is a lightweight Python tool that sits over well-known analysis tools that produce outputs such as tables, plots, and statistical models. This package adds functionality to:","This creates an explicit change in the dynamics so that SDC is something done with researchers rather than to them, and enables more efficient communication with checkers."],"features":["automatically identify potentially disclosive outputs against a range of commonly used disclosure tests;","apply optional disclosure mitigation strategies as requested;","report reasons for applying SDC;","and produce simple summary documents trusted research environment staff can use to streamline their workflow and maintain auditable records."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4258628307b908f83c757ed57c348e32150458529cb42ea80cd2c4dd07f4d236","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T05:59:43.716Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T18:32:56.493Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T17:48:21Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"ACRO is a free and open source tool that supports the semi-automated checking of research outputs (SACRO) for privacy disclosure within secure data environments. SACRO is a framework that applies best-practice principles-based statistical disclosure control (SDC) techniques on-the-fly as researchers conduct their analysis. SACRO is designed to assist human checkers rather than seeking to replace them as with current automated rules-based approaches.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4258628307b908f83c757ed57c348e32150458529cb42ea80cd2c4dd07f4d236","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T18:32:56.493Z"},"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:13:23.792Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T18:32:56.493Z","hash":"4258628307b908f83c757ed57c348e32150458529cb42ea80cd2c4dd07f4d236","originalBytes":4543,"storedBytes":4543,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["acro","research","data","outputs","sacro","see","conda","disclosure","package","python","sdc","checking","dataset","example","notebooks","pypi","researchers","training","